      "side": 1,
      "message": "fpclassify is potentially expensive as it requires transitioning between the ARM FP pipeline and INT pipeline.  Subnormals are not an issue on ARM performance-wise, but they are expensive on x86-64.  Are there any reasons to exclude them?\n https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:external/musl/src/math/__fpclassifyf.c;drc\u003d8dba5486288e719ed290cccefcd932ed32756d7c;l\u003d4\n\nperhaps something like the following (moved to audio_utils).\n\n    inline constexpr float clampVolume(float volume) {\n        // Note: we use explicit comparison to control nan handling.\n        \n        constexpr float maxInternalVolume \u003d 1.f;\n        if (volume \u003e\u003d FLT_MIN) { // minimum normal float\n            if (volume \u003c\u003d maxInternalVolume) return volume; // FP_NORMAL\n            return maxInternalVolume; // FP_INFINITE, FP_NORMAL\n        } \n        return 0.f;  // FP_SUBNORMAL, FP_NAN, FP_ZERO, FP_NORMAL\n    }",
